MiniBBS v2.12b
==============

This is a modified version of HOST.SLC and HCONFIG.SLC written by the auther
of Telix.  The program was modified by Jonathan Rapoport.  It is a great
program to use when your BBS is down, or you want to communicate with someone
easily.

Jonathan Rapoport, Colin Sampaleanu, & EXIS INC. assume no responsibility for
the use of this program, and issue no warrenty.  And are not liable for any
dammages, as a result of the use of this program.

This program requires that you use TELIX v3.00, and greater, and you create a
directory called \MINIBBS\MISC.

To load this program and run it. First load Telix, then press ALT-G and type
in MINIBBS then press ENTER, or type in from DOS   TELIX SMINIBBS, then press
ENTER.  n.b. Make sure that there is an s before MINIBBS.

To configure Mini BBS,  you can use the same method as above, but instead of
typing MINIBBS, type MCONFIG.  This should be done first, as the program will
not work properly if the directories doesn't exist.

n.b.  Jmodem will not work with Telix v3.11, or lower.  This is because it is
      not installed internally, and external protocalls don't work with
      MiniBBS.  Sorry for any enconvience.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MAKE SURE that you have a directory called \MINIBBS\MISC, and have your text,
and batch files in that directory, otherwise they will not be displayed.

n.b. Make sure you run MCONFIG, when you upgrade to this version, as there is
     a different setup than the last version.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Here are all the files that you can create to make your BBS look nicer, but
they are not nessary.

WRONG.PAS    - When a wrong password is entered
FIRST.MSG    - The file displayed before asking for user name
BYEBYE.MSG   - File displayed when the user logs off.
PAGE.ABT     - File displayed, when SysOp doesn't want to chat, or when there
             - is no answer.
FILES.BBS    - Listing of files on your system.
BULLETIN.MSG - Bulletin listing.
BBSNUM.LST   - BBS number listing, ie. ACCUlist.
MESSAGE.LST  - Message file.
NEWUSER.IFO  - New user information file.
EXTRA.IFO    - Extra information file.

MAIN.MNU     - REQUIRED.  THIS IS THE MAIN MENU. comes with MiniBBS, but can be
               changed. If this file does not exist, MiniBBS will work, but the
               user cannot see his options, all he sees is the line that says
               command :  .


The above files MUST be \MINIBBS\MISC, otherwise they will not be displayed.
Most come in the MiniBBS archive.

The change message option, Online program option, and DOS function option have
been changed so that they can be only seen on local mode, and a password is no
longer required.  The keys that were in version 2.01b (for these options) Have
been changed, Please refer to MiniBBS for the keys to use.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Two Batch files needed.

ONLINE.BAT  - Contains information to run a online game (program) when you press
              The online program key. (Set up For BlackJack).

MESSAGE.BAT - Contains information to tell your editor what to do. (Set up for
              Qedit).
 
these files should be in the same directory as the display files.  Examples
are given.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

F1 - To chat automaticaly, any time with the caller.

The menu, when a user calls has been changed.  First is displayes the Main menu
file, then is says the LOCAL functions.  The Local functions are ONLY displayed
on the local side of the system.  ie. If MiniBBS is on, and running on your
system, you will se them.  They are ONLY avaliable on local mode.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

F3 - DOS functions.  Please see your Telix manual for help with DOS commands.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Here are the passwords that you MUST configure before running MINIBBS.
configure them with the script file MCONFIG.

Level 1 Password.  Regular user password.

Level 2 (SysOp) Password.  Sysop access password.

Upload password.  The pass to upload a file.

Download password. The pass to d-load a file.

Sysop access password.  The pass to Shell to DOS, Shut down, and display usage
                        log.

Upload directory.  Where the uploaded files will go.

Download directory.  Where user is allowed to d-load files from.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Sysop function bar:

I added a little bar that is displayed under the menu.  This bar is only
shown on the local monitor.  And the functions are only avaliable to the
person on the local side of the computer.  The functions are self
explanitory, and very easy to use.

